{"parentUuid":"d6b97302-bef9-4056-b8fc-2469ecc37b51","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_018y6wMQ7vi3kuDTm5Mi6aNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WM2GVJeTBEsq5kE56ePJgv","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"DDOpt decision diagram based optimization solver 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7191,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":182,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7191},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":182,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy6uuJF98xFnBojTMyN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddea4357-77c4-4a8a-9915-aabf1487e343","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:11.581Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d6b97302-bef9-4056-b8fc-2469ecc37b51","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G8KP8h2HtkbWLAwNY2bNcB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"decision diagram optimization Bergman Hooker MDD survey 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An Introduction to Decision Diagrams for Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/DD_TutORial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"INFORMS 2024 © 2024 INFORMS|isbn 978-0-xxxxxxx-x-x\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DD_TutORial_2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Optimization - CMU\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/mdd/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - vcoppe/mdd-solver: Discrete optimization solver based on Multi-valued Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/vcoppe/mdd-solver\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Discrete Optimization with Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/291425048_Discrete_Optimization_with_Decision_Diagrams\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Manipulating MDD Relaxations for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353505_Manipulating_MDD_Relaxations_for_Combinatorial_Optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Discrete Optimization: A Survey of Recent Advances\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/orijoc/v34y2022i4p2271-2295.html\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Discrete Optimization with Decision Diagrams | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Discrete-Optimization-with-Decision-Diagrams-Bergman-Cir%C3%A9/cf5f92b2fc034c6468d41c75f3346c890123fc9d\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Discrete Optimization: A Survey of Recent Advances\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/359410432_Decision_Diagrams_for_Discrete_Optimization_A_Survey_of_Recent_Advances\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-030-54621-2_712-1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant resources on decision diagram optimization research by Bergman and Hooker:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nBergman, Cire, Van Hoeve, and Hooker developed a novel branch-and-bound method where relaxed decision diagrams provide dual bounds for combinatorial optimization.\n\n**Recent Publications (2024-2025):**\n\nThe search results include:\n\n1. **2024 INFORMS Tutorial**: A comprehensive tutorial on decision diagrams for optimization addressing MDD propagation algorithms for various constraint types\n\n2. **Survey on Recent Advances**: Recent 2024 publications include work on flow-based formulations for parallel machine scheduling using decision diagrams and decision diagram-based branch-and-bound with caching for dominance and suboptimality detection\n\n3. **Application Areas**: Decision diagrams have been applied to stochastic optimization, Benders decomposition, pricing in column generation, post-optimality analysis, and domain-specific applications\n\nThe research demonstrates that the decision diagram-based branch-and-bound method evaluated on classical combinatorial optimization problems obtained competitive results, with approaches outperforming state-of-the-art integer programming solvers in several cases.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e8018611-8baa-4db9-b8bc-08f55f7f9074","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:17.632Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6b97302-bef9-4056-b8fc-2469ecc37b51","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ddea4357-77c4-4a8a-9915-aabf1487e343","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WM2GVJeTBEsq5kE56ePJgv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DDOpt decision diagram based optimization solver 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An Introduction to Decision Diagrams for Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/DD_TutORial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ctjandra/ddopt-bounds\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ctjandra/ddopt-bounds\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Optimization - a4cp.org\",\"url\":\"https://a4cp.org/sites/default/files/andre_augusto_cire_-_decision_diagrams_for_optimization.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Optimization - CMU\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/mdd/\"},{\"title\":\"Discrete Optimization with Decision Diagrams | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2015.0648\"},{\"title\":\"Selected Topics in Network Optimization: Aligning Binary Decision Diagrams for a Facility Location Problem and a Search Method for Dynamic Shortest Path Interdiction\",\"url\":\"https://open.clemson.edu/all_dissertations/2915/\"},{\"title\":\"DDOPT 2024\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/ddopt-2024\"},{\"title\":\"CODD: A Decision Diagram-based Solver for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/CODD-ECAI2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Graph Coloring with Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/8215.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Discrete Optimization John Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://icaps16.icaps-conference.org/proceedings/tutorials/tutorial4.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about DDOpt and decision diagram-based optimization solvers:\n\n## DDOpt: Decision Diagram-Based Optimization Solver\n\nDDOpt is a framework that generates dual bounds from relaxed decision diagrams with the goal of improving pruning throughout the branch-and-bound tree of a MIP solver, using Lagrangian relaxation and constraint propagation to take into account constraints that are more difficult to tackle with decision diagrams.\n\nThe approach has been tested on the independent set problem with and without knapsack side constraints. The main requirements are SCIP 5.0.1, ConicBundle 0.3.11, Boost, and a C++ compiler in a Linux environment.\n\n## Related Decision Diagram Optimization Tools\n\nThe search also revealed other decision diagram-based solvers and frameworks:\n\n- The DDOPT symposium brings together researchers interested in methods, algorithms, theory, applications, and tools for optimization that are related to decision diagram technology.\n\n- The CODD library provides generic functionality which, when instantiated with model-specific state description and manipulation functions produces a full-blown implementation.\n\nLimited-width decision diagrams can be deployed as relaxations to provide bounds on the objective, and as restrictions to provide feasible solutions, naturally applied in concert to provide an exact solver similar to traditional branch and bound methods.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"77722737-f348-4b2f-9d39-ae9ad8a281ff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:19.214Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ddea4357-77c4-4a8a-9915-aabf1487e343","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
