{"parentUuid":"3c8675e2-04b9-4475-ba19-ea3b19785ec6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AzhWZEJrYP3rdYncPvG5xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L31R9b6Vy4ccgYgRe1E4Zr","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"multivalued decision diagram MDD CP-SAT integration relaxed restricted bounds"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4186,"cache_read_input_tokens":23036,"output_tokens":162,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4186},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":23036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4186,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy8ef5JRZDSco3KF3ch","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb662bbe-1767-4a0e-9ba6-7539e21cfe7f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:34.597Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3c8675e2-04b9-4475-ba19-ea3b19785ec6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZxUYGCczerNHxKqHxnr2V","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"decision diagram 2D packing rectangle placement bin packing 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"Online calculator: 2D Bin Packing Problem Solver\",\"url\":\"https://planetcalc.com/8634/\"},{\"title\":\"Multidimensional Bin Packing and Other Related Problems: A Survey ∗\",\"url\":\"https://tetali.math.gatech.edu/PUBLIS/CKPT.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"},{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement Learning Schema\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.09677v1\"},{\"title\":\"Neural-Driven Constructive Heuristic for 2D Robotic Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/10/1956\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"The rectangular layout produced by the Maxrects-BL algorithm | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/The-rectangular-layout-produced-by-the-Maxrects-BL-algorithm_fig3_369311169\"},{\"title\":\"On the 2D Demand Bin Packing Problem: Hardness and Approximation Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.13347v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant topics related to your query about decision diagrams, 2D packing, rectangle placement, and bin packing. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## 2D Bin Packing and Rectangle Placement\n\nThe two-dimensional bin packing problem (2D-BPP) is a classical combinatorial NP-hard problem with the objective to pack a set of items (small rectangles) in the minimum number of bins (larger rectangles).\n\n## Recent Approaches (2025)\n\nA recent 2025 study addresses the two-dimensional weakly homogeneous Bin Packing Problem in robotic packing contexts, proposing a novel neural-driven constructive heuristic to overcome limitations of traditional approaches. In 2025, researchers proposed a neural-driven constructive heuristic that leverages a lightweight neural network trained via black-box optimization to dynamically evaluate item placement decisions.\n\n## Decision Diagrams\n\nKell and Hoeve investigated the application of multivalued decision diagrams (MDDs) to multidimensional bin packing. While this reference appears in the search results, it doesn't provide extensive detail about the specific application of decision diagrams to 2D packing problems.\n\n## Common Placement Heuristics\n\nPopular placement heuristics include corner points (locations where item boundaries change direction), extended extreme points including inner placements, and MaxRects, which represents available space as a set of free rectangles.\n\nThe search results show that the field is actively evolving, with recent 2025 work combining neural networks and machine learning approaches with traditional heuristics for 2D rectangle packing and placement problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4f2b442b-e9f7-43ec-b229-bb004fd3dfe5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:42.670Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c8675e2-04b9-4475-ba19-ea3b19785ec6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb662bbe-1767-4a0e-9ba6-7539e21cfe7f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L31R9b6Vy4ccgYgRe1E4Zr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"multivalued decision diagram MDD CP-SAT integration relaxed restricted bounds\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Constraint Store Based on Multivalued Decision Diagrams | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-74970-7_11\"},{\"title\":\"Peel-And-Bound: Generating Stronger Relaxed Bounds with Multivalued Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2022.35\"},{\"title\":\"Submitted to manuscript Multivalued Decision Diagrams for Sequencing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/mdd_sequencing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Diagrams for Optimization - CMU\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/mdd/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization Bounds from Decision Diagrams in Haddock | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-33271-5_11\"},{\"title\":\"Multivalued Decision Diagrams in Optimization - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2011nsf....1130012H/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"[2205.05216] Peel-and-Bound: Generating Stronger Relaxed Bounds with Multivalued Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.05216\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Constraint Store Based on Multivalued Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221633490_A_Constraint_Store_Based_on_Multivalued_Decision_Diagrams\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Peel-and-Bound: Generating Stronger Relaxed Bounds with Multivalued Decision Diagrams\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360538489_Peel-and-Bound_Generating_Stronger_Relaxed_Bounds_with_Multivalued_Decision_Diagrams\"},{\"title\":\"Multivalued Decision Diagrams for Sequencing Problems | Springer Nature Link (formerly SpringerLink)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-10428-7_67\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive search results related to your query. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Overview of Multivalued Decision Diagrams (MDDs)\n\nA limited-width multivalued decision diagram (MDD) serves as a richer constraint store that reduces to a traditional domain store when the maximum width is one but allows greater pruning of the search tree for larger widths.\n\n## Relaxed and Restricted MDDs\n\nHadzic et al. (2008) and Hoda et al. (2010) developed generic methods for systematically compiling relaxed MDDs. The fundamental idea of their approaches is to construct the diagram in an incremental fashion, associating a particular state information with the MDD nodes so as to indicate how new nodes and arcs should be added to the diagram.\n\nAndersen et al. introduced the concept of a relaxed MDD, which is a diagram of limited size that represents an over-approximation of the feasible solution set of a problem.\n\n## Integration with Optimization and Bounds\n\nBergman et al. (2011, 2012) propose similar techniques for the purpose of obtaining bounds for combinatorial optimization problems, which were shown to be superior to their corresponding continuous relaxations for a wide range of instances.\n\nA smaller diagram that represents an approximation of the problem (a \"relaxation,\" meaning that all possible solutions are represented, along with some others) can provide bounds on the optimal solution value, which are very useful when searching for an optimal solution.\n\n## Recent Developments: Peel-and-Bound\n\nA method called peel-and-bound peels off a sub-graph of previously constructed diagrams and uses it as the initial diagram for subsequent iterations, generating stronger bounds than a branch-and-bound scheme using the same propagators at significantly less computational cost.\n\nHowever, I note that while the search results extensively cover MDDs with constraint programming and optimization, there are no direct results specifically mentioning \"CP-SAT integration\" with MDDs. CP-SAT is Google's constraint programming solver, so you may want to search for more recent literature or technical documentation specific to that solver's implementation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"66fafc3c-24ab-4d67-b50c-edd098597bd9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:44.121Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb662bbe-1767-4a0e-9ba6-7539e21cfe7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"66fafc3c-24ab-4d67-b50c-edd098597bd9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac5c8f6946e43cacc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013Xioz8XbmjbCghXcep5uKT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我已经收集到足够信息，整理输出。\n\n---\n\n# Decision Diagrams 在组合优化的应用调研（2024-2026）\n\n## 1. BDD/MDD/ZDD 基础 + Hooker 学派综述\n\n**三种 DD 各自定位：**\n- **BDD（二元决策图）**：变量是 0/1，把布尔函数压成共享 DAG。逻辑综合、模型检测的老朋友。\n- **MDD（多值决策图）**：变量取多个离散值。Hooker / Hadzic / Andersen 2007 把它从模型检测领域搬进 OR，作为「比域存储更强的约束存储」。\n- **ZDD（零抑制决策图）**：Minato 1993 提出，专门压缩稀疏集合族。适合做「所有满足某条件的子集」枚举，比如独立集、路径、生成树。\n\n**Hooker 学派核心思路（2007 起十多年沉淀）：**\n- 把 DP（动态规划）状态展开成分层 DAG 就得到 exact MDD，但宽度爆炸。\n- **Relaxed MDD**：限定宽度上界 W，合并状态，得到 over-approximation -> 提供对偶界（dual bound）。\n- **Restricted MDD**：限定宽度但删除部分状态，得到 under-approximation -> 提供原始可行解。\n- 二者配合替代 LP 松弛，构成 **DD-based Branch-and-Bound**（Bergman/Cire/van Hoeve/Hooker 2016 *Discrete Optimization with Decision Diagrams*，Springer 那本书是教科书级材料）。\n- 2022 *INFORMS J. Computing* 的综述《Decision Diagrams for Discrete Optimization: A Survey of Recent Advances》总结了过去十年。\n\n**2024 最新综述：** INFORMS 2024 Tutorial *An Introduction to Decision Diagrams for Optimization*（van Hoeve），覆盖到 stochastic、Benders、列生成定价、后优化分析等扩展方向。\n\n## 2. DDOpt / DD-based optimization 现状\n\n- **DDOpt（Tjandra）**：用 Lagrangian relaxation + 约束传播给松弛 DD 加 side constraint，作为 SCIP 的对偶界源。已在独立集 + 背包 side constraint 上验证。技术栈 SCIP 5.0.1 + ConicBundle，C++/Linux。\n- **Peel-and-Bound（Rudich 2022, arXiv 2205.05216）**：每轮从已有 DD 上「剥离」子图作为下轮起点，比标准 B&B 用同样 propagator 的情况下界更紧、计算更便宜。\n- **Parallel DD**（多伦多 Cire 组）：把 B&B 节点的 relaxed/restricted 编译并行化，对大规模实例加速明显。\n- **DDOPT Symposium**（2024 起）：DD 圈年度专场，标志这条线已经有独立社区。\n\n## 3. SymBDD / 工具链\n\n直接叫 SymBDD 的 OR 工具我没搜到主流条目（SymBDD 主要在硬件/SAT 圈用作符号 BDD 操作库）。**OR 圈实际用的工具链：**\n- **CODD（Michel & van Hoeve, ECAI 2024）**：基于状态化 DP 模型规约自动编译 relaxed/restricted DD 嵌入 B&B。设计上「层无关（layer-free）」，按 DAG 而非分层栈跑，比早期实现灵活。在多个组合问题上比 IP/CP 快「数量级」。\n- **mdd-solver（Coppé, GitHub vcoppe/mdd-solver）**：基于 MDD 的离散优化通用求解器，开源 reference 实现。\n- **ddopt-bounds（GitHub ctjandra/ddopt-bounds）**：DDOpt 的实现仓。\n- 老一些的 Haddock（关系约束的 DD 后端）。\n\n## 4. 跟 LCG 的关系\n\nLCG（Stuckey/Chu，Chuffed/MiniZinc 后端）= CP propagator 把 nogood 翻成 SAT 子句，让 SAT 引擎学 + 反向跳跃。\n\n**DD 与 LCG 的交集（关键论文：Abío/Stuckey 等）：**\n- 可以**从 exact 或 relaxed BDD 学子句**注入 SAT 引擎。任何 SAT 冲突分析能学到的子句这种方法都能学到，并且能学出冲突分析单次推不出来的「更强子句」。\n- 因此 DD 不是 LCG 的替代，而是**补充**：DD 给「全局结构性子句源」，LCG 给「冲突驱动学习引擎」。\n- 但目前主流 LCG 实现（Chuffed）并没有把 DD 子句生成做成默认。CP-SAT（Google OR-Tools）走的也是 LCG 路线，但它没暴露 DD 接口。\n\n## 5. 对 placement / packing 的应用\n\n**这是最关键的一节，结论比较冷静：**\n- Kell & van Hoeve 做过 **multidimensional bin packing 的 MDD** 应用（早期工作），但后续没爆发。\n- **2D 矩形 packing / placement 的主流仍是**：Positions-and-Covering MIP、no-overlap CP global constraint、MaxRects 启发式，最近两年大量神经启发式（transformer/RL 做在线 strip packing）。\n- **DD 在 packing 上的劣势**：packing 的状态是「已占据格子集合」，状态空间是 2^(70x70)，relaxed MDD 合并这种几何状态没有自然的 dominance 规则，width 撑不下来。\n- **DD 在 packing 上的优势出现在**：item 序列固定且仅决定位置/旋转的小维问题、或 1D strip packing。\n- ZDD 在「枚举所有合法布局子集」类问题（Knuth Vol. 4 / TAOCP 风格）有效，但我们要的是 max area + min_side 的最优化，不是枚举。\n\n## 总结：是否值得 PoC\n\n**不值得在当前 Phase 3B 投 PoC。** 理由：\n\n1. **几何状态不友好**：70x70 grid + ghost rectangle + 266 mandatory facility 这种 2D 几何耦合，状态合并规则没有标准 DP，relaxed MDD 的 width 控制上不去，对偶界比 LP 强不了多少。\n2. **生态空白**：CP-SAT/OR-Tools 没有 DD 接口，要 DD 就要换 CODD/SCIP+DDOpt 整条工具链，跟现有 Benders（master+binding+routing+flow）+ 校准好的 CP-SAT 拆掉重来，工程量两个数量级以上。\n3. **跟我们已有手段重合度低但收益不明**：我们的瓶颈不是「缺对偶界」，是「外层候选枚举 + 内层 routing/flow 反复打圈」。DD 在「序列化决策」（TSP/调度/排列约束）上提速最明显，对我们的 placement 几何子结构基本不沾边。\n4. **LCG 通道更直接**：如果想往「学到的全局子句」方向走，比起搞 DD 子句生成，更现实的是研究 CP-SAT 现有 nogood/clause learning 的 hint 接口，或在 master 模型里加 implied no-overlap 全局约束。\n\n**保留观察项**：CODD/Peel-and-Bound 这条线如果未来出了「2D rectangle placement 专门的状态合并规则」论文，再回头看；目前作为长期 watchlist 即可，不进 Round 9 候选。\n\nSources:\n- [An Introduction to Decision Diagrams for Optimization (INFORMS Tutorial 2024)](https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/DD_TutORial.pdf)\n- [Decision Diagrams for Optimization - CMU (van Hoeve hub)](https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/mdd/)\n- [Decision Diagrams for Discrete Optimization: A Survey of Recent Advances (IJOC 2022)](https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/orijoc/v34y2022i4p2271-2295.html)\n- [CODD: A Decision Diagram-based Solver for Combinatorial Optimization (ECAI 2024)](https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/vanhoeve/papers/CODD-ECAI2024.pdf)\n- [DDOPT 2024 Symposium](https://sites.google.com/view/ddopt-2024)\n- [DDOpt-bounds GitHub](https://github.com/ctjandra/ddopt-bounds)\n- [mdd-solver GitHub (Coppé)](https://github.com/vcoppe/mdd-solver)\n- [Peel-and-Bound: Stronger Relaxed Bounds with MDDs (CP 2022)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2022.35)\n- [Discrete Optimization with Decision Diagrams (Bergman et al., IJOC)](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2015.0648)\n- [Lazy Clause Generation Reengineered (Stuckey)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-04244-7_29)\n- [Applications of Zero-Suppressed Decision Diagrams (Springer 2024)](https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-79870-2)\n- [Multidimensional Bin Packing Survey (Khan et al.)](https://tetali.math.gatech.edu/PUBLIS/CKPT.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3096,"cache_read_input_tokens":27222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3096,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9jRqzd1E3KmLjr6e2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f42ed849-3de9-4f9c-bbd9-8a206b83aafa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:52.314Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
